  "id": "body-schema",
  "term": "body schema",
  "definition": "Body schema is the mind’s implicit sensorimotor map of the body that is used during movement. It also supports planning and mentally simulating actions, such as imagining rotating one’s own body to judge left and right from an egocentric viewpoint.",
